WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.688 --> 00:00:17.639
When Sir Richard left Sherwood Forest, he didn't travel alone.

2
00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:20.301
A group of Robin's men went with him.

3
00:00:21.542 --> 00:00:27.547
The group headed along a straight highway toward the monastery, so that Sir Richard could pay his debt

4
00:00:27.627 --> 00:00:28.688
to Abbot Vincent.

5
00:00:29.492 --> 00:00:34.955
Far away in the distance rose the towers of the abbey, with tall trees surrounding it.

6
00:00:37.016 --> 00:00:41.199
Meanwhile, inside the abbey, the abbot was holding a big feast.

7
00:00:41.879 --> 00:00:48.343
He wore soft robes of fine silk, a black velvet cap, and a heavy gold chain around his

8
00:00:48.403 --> 00:00:53.846
neck. While he ate, a falcon sat on the arm of his large chair.

9
00:00:54.706 --> 00:00:57.888
The Sheriff of Nottingham sat on one side of the abbot.

10
00:00:58.976 --> 00:01:01.237
His purple robe was trimmed with fur.

11
00:01:02.398 --> 00:01:05.039
A famous judge sat on the other side of the abbot.

12
00:01:05.599 --> 00:01:09.080
The judge's clothes were dark and plain, but he was quite happy.

13
00:01:09.821 --> 00:01:14.583
The abbot had just paid him eighty gold coins for helping to ruin Sir Richard.

14
00:01:14.603 --> 00:01:20.025
"Are you sure you'll get Sir Richard's castle and all his land?"

15
00:01:20.445 --> 00:01:21.826
the sheriff asked the abbot.

16
00:01:21.846 --> 00:01:26.708
"Oh, yes," said Abbot Vincent with a sinister smile.

17
00:01:27.936 --> 00:01:29.798
He took a long drink of wine.

18
00:01:29.818 --> 00:01:33.401
"Sir Richard doesn't know I've been watching him closely.

19
00:01:35.003 --> 00:01:37.345
He has no money to pay his debt."

20
00:01:39.367 --> 00:01:44.671
Suddenly there came the sound of a horse's hooves clattering as it entered the courtyard below.

21
00:01:44.691 --> 00:01:46.593
"See who that is!"

22
00:01:47.114 --> 00:01:48.775
the abbot commanded a servant.

23
00:01:50.136 --> 00:01:51.798
The servant looked out the window.

24
00:01:51.818 --> 00:01:53.780
"It's a knight with some men.

25
00:01:55.300 --> 00:01:58.941
The knight is dressed plainly, but the men are well armed with bows and arrows."

26
00:02:03.102 --> 00:02:05.883
"That must be Sir Richard," said the abbot.

27
00:02:05.903 --> 00:02:09.684
"But why has he brought so many men?"

28
00:02:10.024 --> 00:02:12.045
The judge was suddenly nervous.

29
00:02:12.065 --> 00:02:13.645
"Will he attack us?

30
00:02:14.345 --> 00:02:18.126
Abbot, maybe you should give him more time to pay his debt."

31
00:02:18.146 --> 00:02:21.027
"Don't worry," scoffed the abbot.

32
00:02:22.007 --> 00:02:23.788
"This knight is very gentle.

33
00:02:24.608 --> 00:02:25.889
He won't hurt anyone."

34
00:02:27.649 --> 00:02:29.490
Just then the door swung open.

35
00:02:30.310 --> 00:02:35.212
Sir Richard entered the room with his hands folded and his head bowed humbly.

36
00:02:35.993 --> 00:02:38.314
His men waited by the door with their weapons.

37
00:02:38.994 --> 00:02:43.776
The knight approached the table and knelt on one knee in front of Abbot Vincent.

38
00:02:43.796 --> 00:02:45.997
"Where's my money?"

39
00:02:46.317 --> 00:02:47.337
demanded the abbot.

40
00:02:48.798 --> 00:02:50.739
Sir Richard's cheeks turned red.

41
00:02:50.759 --> 00:02:54.080
"Please show me some mercy," he said softly.

42
00:02:54.932 --> 00:02:56.433
"I don't have any money."

43
00:02:57.133 --> 00:03:00.114
Abbot Vincent said nothing, but he looked angry.

44
00:03:00.915 --> 00:03:02.735
Sir Richard appealed to the judge.

45
00:03:02.755 --> 00:03:05.776
"Please, sir, can you help me?"

46
00:03:07.117 --> 00:03:11.579
The abbot was right—this quiet knight didn't seem threatening at all.

47
00:03:12.679 --> 00:03:16.361
So the judge boldly said, "The money is due today.

48
00:03:17.121 --> 00:03:18.882
You must pay it now!"

49
00:03:19.662 --> 00:03:22.043
Sir Richard was not ready to give up.

50
00:03:22.063 --> 00:03:24.124
"What about you, Sheriff?

51
00:03:24.844 --> 00:03:25.785
Can you help me?"

52
00:03:25.805 --> 00:03:30.528
"This really is no business of mine, but I'll do what I can."

53
00:03:30.949 --> 00:03:36.132
The sheriff nudged the abbot with a knee and whispered, "Can you reduce the amount the knight owes

54
00:03:36.172 --> 00:03:42.117
you?" "All right," muttered the abbot to Sir Richard.

55
00:03:42.137 --> 00:03:48.261
"Give me three hundred pounds, Sir Richard, and I'll consider your debt paid."

56
00:03:50.123 --> 00:03:51.424
Sir Richard shook his head.

57
00:03:51.964 --> 00:03:55.365
"I'm sorry, but I can't pay three hundred pounds now, Abbot.

58
00:03:55.885 --> 00:03:57.886
Please give me another year to pay my debt."

59
00:03:58.786 --> 00:04:00.046
"Not another day!"

60
00:04:00.466 --> 00:04:02.187
Abbot Vincent said sternly.

61
00:04:02.207 --> 00:04:06.528
"Either pay it today or everything you own is mine."

62
00:04:08.529 --> 00:04:09.689
Sir Richard stood up.

63
00:04:10.229 --> 00:04:13.410
The gentle knight suddenly looked stern and furious.

64
00:04:13.430 --> 00:04:15.871
"I've tried to be polite to you!"

65
00:04:16.211 --> 00:04:16.751
he snapped.

66
00:04:16.771 --> 00:04:19.812
"But you haven't even offered me anything to eat.

67
00:04:20.532 --> 00:04:23.134
I'll pay three hundred pounds and not a penny more!"

68
00:04:23.874 --> 00:04:27.217
The judge trembled at Sir Richard's angry tone.

69
00:04:27.237 --> 00:04:29.258
"Please, gentlemen!

70
00:04:29.758 --> 00:04:32.080
Let's speak kindly to one another.

71
00:04:32.620 --> 00:04:34.542
There's no need to argue."

72
00:04:35.903 --> 00:04:38.804
Sir Richard motioned to one of his men to come forward.

73
00:04:39.365 --> 00:04:43.788
The biggest, strongest-looking man brought a leather bag to Sir Richard.

74
00:04:44.288 --> 00:04:49.452
The knight opened it and dumped a stream of gold coins onto the table in front of the

75
00:04:49.552 --> 00:04:51.072
abbot. "There, Abbot!

76
00:04:51.553 --> 00:04:53.774
I've paid my debt, and now I'm through with you!"

77
00:04:54.494 --> 00:04:56.495
Sir Richard turned and stormed away.

78
00:04:57.835 --> 00:05:01.357
Abbot Vincent was angry that he'd lost Sir Richard's property.

79
00:05:01.897 --> 00:05:03.298
He scowled at the sheriff.

80
00:05:03.318 --> 00:05:08.920
"Thanks to you, Sir Richard paid only three hundred pounds!"

81
00:05:11.481 --> 00:05:13.742
But the Sheriff of Nottingham wasn't listening.

82
00:05:14.582 --> 00:05:17.804
He was staring at the huge man who'd carried the gold.

83
00:05:18.748 --> 00:05:21.810
"Why, I know you—you're Reynold Greenleaf!"

84
00:05:22.230 --> 00:05:23.031
cried the sheriff.

85
00:05:23.051 --> 00:05:24.852
"My servant!"

86
00:05:24.872 --> 00:05:27.294
"Greetings, Sheriff!"

87
00:05:27.814 --> 00:05:29.495
Little John said with a grin.

88
00:05:29.515 --> 00:05:34.398
"I'll be sure to tell Robin Hood about the good deed you did today!"

89
00:05:35.159 --> 00:05:41.363
Then he turned and followed Sir Richard from the room, leaving the sheriff looking pale and stunned.
